items: orphan-fixedin-lands-red
paths: file:.githooks/pre-push file:tests/BUGS.md
scope: |
  bugs-index-gate catches an orphaned `fixed-in:` only AFTER it lands, so main goes red for
  everyone until the owner notices. THREE entries in two days: rust-backend-two-tests-red…,
  lower-has-six-hand-written-Expr-walkers…, smoke-suite-over-its-own-budget. The cause is
  structural, not carelessness — the SHA is written into the entry in the same commit as the fix,
  and the rebase-and-push loop then rewrites it. Catch it in pre-push, where it costs the author
  one retry instead of costing everyone a red suite.
next: plan the task into SPRINT.md, then implement
